Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

BRepGProp_Gauss: the volume and area integration integrates across the
joints of each face's loop of pcurves, so that every loop closes in the
face's parameters, and the volume integration integrates the ribbon from
each edge's curve on a face to its 3D curve, so that the faces close along
the edges' 3D curves (mitcad#2284, follow-up of mitcad#2267, GitHub
mitcad/Mitcad#463).

The case: a ring (a torus) joined with blades, triangles and rods read
from a STEP file. Its common with the union has 40 faces on the ring's own
surfaces, cut where the other bodies cross the torus. The common measured
21135.163838, 21135.164173 and 21135.077405 mm3 about its middle and two
points a diagonal away along X and Z, the ring 21135.140975 about each: a
spread of 4.1e-6 relative with the point it is integrated about, where a
closed shell has one volume about every point. The common's shell closes
in space: its faces' shares of the ring's surface from their edges' 3D
curves sum to (2.3e-14, -1.9e-14, 4.1e-11) mm2, through their pcurves with
the joints closed to (-6.4e-12, -6.7e-14, -4.2e-11), while their normals
integrated over their areas summed to (-1.53e-6, 1.08e-4, 3.96e-4).

The cause: Compute integrates a face by Green's theorem in its parameters
along its edges' pcurves (the domain's edges in their orientation in the
forward face): at each point of a pcurve the integrand is integrated in u
from the face's lowest u to the point, and that along the pcurve against
dv. That is the integral over the domain the pcurves bound only where each
pcurve starts at the parameters where the one before it ends. The
common's pcurves meet at their vertices within the vertices' tolerance but
apart along v (the section edges' and the ring's edges' curves on one
face end at their own parameters of the vertex): each such joint left out
a strip from the lowest u to the joint, as wide as the joint's gap along
v, up to the ring's circumference long on the torus face reaching round
the ring (159 joints, apart by up to 4.07e-8 along v, 9.17e-8 mm in
space). The strips left out summed to (-1.53e-6, 1.08e-4, 3.96e-4) mm2,
the whole of the integrated normals' sum; with every face's loop closed
at its joints the common measured 21135.140974536, 21135.140974536 and
21135.140974539 mm3 about the three points, the ring 21135.140974537.

JointNodes pairs, in each wire of the forward face, each edge use's end
(its pcurve's point at its end in the edge's orientation) with the start
of a use there at the same vertex not yet paired, the nearest in the
parameters. A joint whose two points and middle lie on the surface within
the vertex's tolerance of it (not a period apart, not across the domain)
and whose points differ along v by more than 1e-14 of the face's v range
(at least 1e-14, below that the gap is the parameters' rounding) is
integrated as the straight segment from the end to the start: Gauss
points along the segment and, at each, in u from the face's lowest u over
the surface's u knot spans, the parameters kept within the face's bounds
as the pcurves' points are. The three Compute methods that integrate over
a domain (the adaptive one, and the non-adaptive volume and area ones) add
those nodes' integrand to the face's sums after the domain's edges. A
joint apart only along u adds nothing, and faces whose pcurves meet at
their vertices exactly are integrated as before.

Closing the loops alone measures each face over the domain its pcurves
bound. Where a pcurve lies off its edge's 3D curve (within the edge's
tolerance: an approximated section curve's pcurve on a blend, say), the
face reaches past the edge or stops short of it, and the face beside it on
another surface, bounded by its own curve of the edge, does not meet it.
An integration along the pcurves alone happened to hide such an offset
where the pcurve runs along u (its v offset reads nothing); with the
loops closed alone, two roundings mitred at a short edge
(geometry.suite.fillet_corners, their blends cut by each other along
approximated curves) measured 16.0707129 mm3 removed against 16.0693324
from booleans of the analytic shapes, past the test's 5e-5. RibbonNodes
integrates, for the volume (and its moments), the ribbon from each edge's
curve on the face A(t) to its 3D curve C(t), R(t, s) = A(t) + s (C(t) -
A(t)), oriented with the face (the face's orientation in the shape, the
edge's in the face): at 8 Gauss points on each of the 3D curve's C2
intervals (at least 4 pieces, at most 32) and 2 across. Faces and ribbons
together close along the edges' 3D curves, the remaining holes at the
vertices of the order of the tolerance squared. Two faces on one surface
sharing their edge's pcurve have opposite ribbons that cancel. Only edges
whose tolerance is above the confusion tolerance (1e-7 mm) are looked at
(an edge's curves lie within its tolerance of each other, so a tighter
edge's ribbon holds nothing the integration can tell), and of those only
edges whose curve on the face lies off the 3D curve by more than 1e-7 mm
at one of five points; degenerated edges, edges without a 3D curve and
edges not SameParameter have none; the area is not changed by ribbons. A
shape whose edges all lie within 1e-7 mm costs one tolerance lookup per
edge. The shape is left as it is: no curve is moved, no tolerance
changed.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2284.
